Krita Nova 09 - palm rejection

Touch on the canvas is ignored while the pen is in use, so a resting hand
neither paints (touch painting) nor pans/zooms/rotates the canvas.

1. KisPalmRejection (libs/ui/input): an application event filter that tracks
   the pen - press/release, moves (incl. hover) and enter/leave proximity.
   The pen counts as "in use" while it is down, while it is in proximity
   (capped at 5 s without pen events, for drivers that never send "leave"),
   and for a grace period after its last event (default 500 ms).
2. Touches larger than a fingertip (default 18 mm, from the reported contact
   ellipse and the screen's physical DPI) are treated as a palm. Only works on
   screens that report contact size; unknown size (0) is never rejected.
3. KisInputManager: a touch sequence is rejected as a whole at TouchBegin, so
   the shortcut matcher always sees balanced begin/end events. If the pen
   comes into use or a palm-sized contact appears during a running sequence,
   the touch action is cancelled and the rest of the sequence is ignored.
4. Configure Krita > General > Tools, below "Touch Pressure Sensitivity":
   on/off, delay (ms), large-contact check and its size (mm).
   kritarc: palmRejectionEnabled, palmRejectionDelay,
   palmRejectionLargeContacts, palmRejectionMaxContactMm.

